### 4. The OwnerRepository — query methods

Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`

Methods available:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName)`
- `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName, Pageable pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int id)`
- `void save(Owner owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()`
- `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner owner)`

There is NO `findByHouseholdId`, NO count method, and no household-specific query anywhere. I grepped the repository package (interface + `jdbc/`, `jpa/`, `springdatajpa/` implementations) for `householdId`, `household`, `namesake`, and `count` — no matches. Any household-member counting today is done in-memory by iterating `findAll()` (as `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold` and `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` do).

Implementations (for reference, all mirror the interface):
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`
- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`

